hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24090","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Isa, informed to us Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Muhayyisah, from his father, that he sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning hiring the cupper, so he forbade him from it. Then he kept asking him about it until he said to him: Feed it to your water-carrying camel, and feed your slaves with it."
"24091","Narrated to us Ishaq, he is Ibn Isa, narrated to us Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, that a she-camel of al-Bara entered a walled garden and spoiled in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that upon the owners of walled gardens is guarding them by day, and what livestock spoil by night is liable upon their owners."
"24092","Narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Saidah ibn Muhayyisah ibn Masud, he said: He had a slave cupper called Abu Taybah, earning much earnings. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of the cupper, he sought license of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning him, but he refused him. So he kept speaking to him about it and mentioning the need, until he said to him: Throw his earnings into the belly of your water-carrying camel."
"24093","Narrated to us Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Saad ibn Muhayyisah, that Muhayyisah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the earnings of a cupper of his, so he forbade him from it. So he kept speaking to him until he said: Feed it to your water-carrying camel, and feed your slaves with it."
"24094","Narrated to us Sufyan, he said: And al-Zuhri heard it from Said ibn al-Musayyab and Haram ibn Saad ibn Muhayyisah, that a she-camel of al-Bara ibn Azib entered the walled garden of a people and spoiled it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged guarding of property upon its owners by day, and upon the owners of livestock what it hits by night."
"24095","Narrated to us Yazid, informed to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Saidah ibn Muhayyisah ibn Masud, from his father, from his grandfather Muhayyisah ibn Masud, he said: He had a slave cupper. And he mentioned the hadith."
"24096","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, from his father, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the earnings of the cupper, so he forbade him. So he repeated to him, and he forbade him. So he mentioned his need, and he said: Feed your water-carrying camel, and feed it to your slaves."
"24097","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, from his father, that a she-camel of al-Bara ibn Azib entered the walled garden of a man and spoiled it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged upon the owners of property guarding it by day, and upon the owners of livestock guarding it by night."
"24098","Narrated to us Yazid, informed to us Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, from his father, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the earnings of the cupper, so he forbade him from it. So he mentioned the need to him, and he said: Feed it to your water-carrying camels."
"24099","Narrated to us Abd al-Samad, narrated to us Hisham, from Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Ayyub, that a man of the Ansar narrated to him, called Muhayyisah: He had a slave cupper, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked him from his earnings. So he said: Shall I not feed with it orphans of mine? He said: No. He said: Shall I not give charity with it? He said: No. So he licensed him to feed it to his water-carrying camel."
